    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0576" n="478" xml:id="pg478"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Cambon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 326.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your courteous note of the 19th instant, expressing the thanks of
                    your Government for the courtesy shown by Rear-Admiral Schley, U. S. N., to the
                    distressed French steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Bretagne.</hi></p>
                <p>A translation of your note is to-day sent to my colleague, the Secretary of the
                    Navy, who will, I am sure, be greatly pleased at your Government’s appreciation
                    of Admiral Schley’s act.</p>
                <p>Accept, excellency, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
